sequenceDiagram
    accTitle: Preview, stage, notch, meld, and revert
    accDescr: An operator reads research and previews a candidate without mutation. The accepted version is staged as an inactive index member. A mediated notch promotes it and marks affected truth for validation. Meld realizes the selected version, and a later notch can deliberately restore the retained prior member.

    actor Operator as Operator / agent
    participant Research as MutationResearch
    participant Conduit as Conduit + SpellIndex
    participant Control as Frame DevOps
    participant Runtime as Meld

    Operator->>Research: residence + source + impact
    Operator->>Research: preview_candidate(code)
    Research-->>Operator: diff + radius + verdict
    Operator->>Conduit: bind_inactive(candidate)
    Conduit-->>Operator: staged member id
    Operator->>Conduit: notch_spell(candidate)
    Conduit->>Control: admit notch transaction
    Control-->>Conduit: scopes granted
    Conduit->>Conduit: park old · select new · mark dirty
    Operator->>Conduit: meld(new member)
    Conduit->>Runtime: validate/recompile if required
    Runtime-->>Operator: selected live instance
    opt deliberate revert
        Operator->>Conduit: notch_spell(previous member)
        Conduit->>Control: admit reverse selection change
        Control-->>Conduit: scopes granted
    end
